<article class="env-definition" id="06NZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06NZ">Definition <span data-tag="06NZ">8.11.1</span>.</a> A <em>gerbe</em> over a site $\mathcal{C}$ is a category $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ over $\mathcal{C}$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ is a stack in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$ (see Definition <a href="/tag/02ZI" data-tag="02ZI">8.5.1</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ there exists a covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ in $\mathcal{C}$ such that $\mathcal{S}_{U_ i}$ is nonempty, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ and $x, y \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{S}_ U)$ there exists a covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ in $\mathcal{C}$ such that $x|_{U_ i} \cong y|_{U_ i}$ in $\mathcal{S}_{U_ i}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>